-	// 68 00 00 00 00          push     <index>
-	// E9 E0 FF FF FF          jmp      <handler>
-	uint8_t code[16] = {0x68, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0xE9, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90};
+	// LOCAL CHANGE (obSCEne): return 0 instead of terminating the process.
+	//
+	// Upstream, an unresolved import is patched to one of these trampolines, which pushes its
+	// relocation index and jumps to RelocateHandler - which prints a stack trace and calls
+	// EXIT(). Calling any unimplemented function therefore kills the process.
+	//
+	// That is defensible for running games: a title that reaches an unimplemented function is
+	// not going to work, and failing loudly beats failing subtly. It is incompatible with a
+	// conformance probe, whose entire job is to call functions and record what came back.
+	// obSCEne dies at the first one - `puts`, in its own output fallback chain - before a
+	// single check has run.
+	//
+	// The guest arrives here through an ordinary `call`, so [rsp] is already the guest return
